smem layout    : SmemLayout::Swizzle128 { lbo_bytes: 16, swapped: false } (every row; the reading the 2026-08-10 sweep settled on hardware)
multicast rule : a .multicast::cluster copy of n bytes performs complete-tx of n on EVERY destination
                 CTA's mbarrier -- it does not divide n among them -- so a c-way split multicast of A
                 plus one own B tile is still tile_a + tile_b per CTA. The clustered and un-clustered
                 rows therefore declare the SAME expect_tx, reached by different arithmetic.
