---- wgmma_config_sweep: correctness, before a single timed launch ----
Every row runs at N = 2 x its own BN, so a clustered row's two CTAs hold DIFFERENT N halves of the same
M tile and each of its A halves has to arrive by multicast from its peer. A multicast defect is silently
wrong data on half the accumulator rows, so the verdict is `==` against an f64 reference over exact-integer
operands, never a tolerance. A fast wrong kernel must not post a timing.
